label 2.14 Rescue Soldier3
With the suppressive fire coming front the sap, as well as from the front lines which have joined in to help, and the momentary stop of mortar rounds, you make it back to the sap and hurl yourself into it, pulling the injured soldier with you.
You roll onto your back and pull your knees to your chest, shaking uncontrollably. Suddenly a pair of very strong hands grab you, lift your body, and pull you out of the sap. The man then brings you into his arms and rocks you like a child.
Sgt Fitzgerald\: Easy son, easy. You’re okay.\
\
You feel your body relax as the Platoon Sergeant soothes you.\
