label 3.1A1
You can’t recall falling asleep. The next morning you awake, get your gear back on, and head out of the dugout for stand to, followed by the morning’s inspection. When 2Lt Holmes comes up to you he’s smiling.
2Lt Holmes\: You’re out of uniform, Lance Corporal.\
\
You\: Sir?\
\
He extends his right hand and you grasp it, his left hand producing a large, single wool chevron.
2Lt Holmes\: Long overdue… Congratulations. Keep it up and you’ll be a section commander soon enough.
You\: Thank-you, Sir!\
\
Sgt Fitzgerald walks up next and gives you his characteristic smack on the arm that nearly knocks you over and nods in approval.
Once everyone is dismissed, Cpl Barron takes you aside.\
\
Cpl Barron\: Well, you’re now Section 2IC. That means you’ll be helping me do the inspections and supervising work details.
