Nearing the barbed wire just before the enemy trench, you take aim and shoot at another German soldier. While you do manage to hit your target, another German tosses a grenade that lands at your feet and explodes, killing you and the men beside you.
set {chosen_path} = "Death 24"
[end_timeline]
label A16A
You take aim at the nearest helmet in the distance and fire a shot but it’s impossible to tell if you hit the soldier. You reload and advance all by muscle memory.
- Shoot at the German Soldiers
	set {chosen_path} = "D16C"
- Rush forward with your bayonet
	set {chosen_path} = "D16A"
- Throw a Grenade
	set {chosen_path} = "A16B"
[end_timeline]
label A16B
Grabbing Brad by his webbing, you crouch and lift him up, positioning his torso onto your shoulders. His body rises off the ground.
An officer approaches you and, seeing that you’ve brought a wounded soldier, immediately calls for aid. Meanwhile, you roll Brad onto his back and lay beside him, trying to catch your breath.
Many years later, you stand in a well-kept graveyard before rows of white-grey gravestones, wearing a navy-blue blazer, grey trousers, medals gleaming in the early morning sun. Your family - children and grandchildren - are with you. 
In your mind’s eye, you can see your friend as he once was - young, energized, and optimistic. Even though he died so many years ago, it feels as if he is watching you. Your body straightens and your right hand comes up in a salute.
- Shoot at the German Soldiers
