label A21
As you take hold of the lewis gun, head to the opening, and proceed to fire on any German soldiers that you see. After a minute, you notice that several enemy soldiers are coming from a distant communication line, so you focus your fire there, suppressing any further advance.
Eventually, you are joined by a wounded 2Lt Holmes and Sgt Fitzgerald. Unfortunately, Cpl Barron was killed in the attack.
The next day, you are promoted to the rank of Corporal and made Section Commander. 2Lt Holmes also notes your courage and quick thinking, submitting you for an honour.
You serve until the end of the war, rising to the rank of Sergeant and retire a decorated veteran of The Great War.
Congratulations, you beat the odds and not only managed to survive, but end your service with distinction. \
\
The End
