[end_timeline]
label D17B
You keep tugging and hitting the bolt, trying to get it to loose. A German soldier enters through the back door, sees you, and tosses a grenade behind you before closing the door. You turn and see the bomb, which then explodes, killing you instantly. \
\
The End
set {chosen_path} = "Death 29"
[end_timeline]
label D16
As you carefully make your way towards the opening of the pill box, you bring your rifle up and unload into the gun crew. You manage to take out three men but a fourth, further back in the enclosure, raises a pistol and fires three rounds into your chest. You fall back, dead. \
\
The End
set {chosen_path} = "Death 30"
[end_timeline]
label D17C
You pull at the loose casing, hitting it a few times with your fist, succeeding in getting it out. Again, you start firing into an advancing group of German soldiers.You hit them all but one manages to toss a grenade before your bullets strike him down.
The grenade spins towards the narrow slit opening of the pill box, prematurely detonating just outside of the structure. The concrete absorbs much of the blast, but you and the machine gun are both sent backwards from the remainder of the kinetic energy.
Ears ringing and vision blurred, it’s a struggle to remain semi-conscious. The entrance to the pill box flings open and two German soldiers rush in. One presses a boot onto your chest, cracking ribs and forcing the air out of your lungs. The muzzle of his Gewehr 98 is set right between your eyes.
German\: Du hast meine Freunde getötet!\
\
You have no idea what he said - you can’t even take your last breath.
BANG!
A shot rings out, followed by another. You stay frozen, bracing yourself for the bullet, and then realize the weight on your chest is gone. You take in a desperate lung full of air, your cracked ribs causing incredible pain.\
\
Brad\: Hey chum, thought I’d bare a hand!
You manage a weak smile before passing out from the strain. You awaken in hospital with bandages covering your eyes. A nursing sister explains that Brad had managed to get you medical attention and that your eyes had been damaged by the exploding grenade. Next, the doctor arrives and slowly removes your bandages.
You open your eyes – your vision is blurry but after several minutes, it remains unchanged. Everything around you his fuzzy – you can make out colours and shapes but details are obscure. While not blind, your vision is permanently impaired. You are honourably discharged and sent back home.
Thankfully, Brad survives the war and returns a year later, remaining a lifelong friend who assists you in daily life. While living with the impairment is challenging, you adjust to your new life, grateful to have survived the war.  
set {chosen_path} = "End 6"
[end_timeline]
label D17D
The jam is too hard to dislodge and so you make the split-second decision to grab the Lewis Gun. Diving for the weapon you scoop it up into your arms just as a stick grenade lands behind you.
Noticing the threat, you drop the machine gun and pick-up the grenade, tossing it towards the pillbox’s opening. Unfortunately, it detonates only feet from your hand, killing you instantly.
The End
set {chosen_path} = "Deeath 31"
[end_timeline]
label D17E
Deciding that the jam is too hard to dislodge, you decide instead to switch to your Lee Enfield. You lift the rifle, work the bolt, take aim at the nearest approaching German soldier, and fire.
Repeating the drill, you take out another soldier, and then another, methodically dropping the advancing force one by one. But there are too many – as you duck down and load another magazine, a stick grenade lands inside the pillbox.
You dive forward to scoop it up and toss it back out the opening when two more grenades land inside the shelter. Defiant to the end, you throw it back at the enemy, seeing it explode just before the two inside the pillbox detonate, killing you.
The End
set {Dialogic} = "Death 32"
[end_timeline]